    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that breakdown. I'm curious about the specific mechanics of the \"failure\" state. When the lecithin barrier fails and the emulsion breaks, is it primarily due to the protonation of the head groups disrupting the electrostatic repulsion, or is it more of a physical displacement of the surfactant by the acid? Could you go into more detail on the kinetics of that breakdown?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
